# OpenCL, for ggml's GPU backend on Adreno. Two repositories because the API
# and the loader that finds a driver for it are separately versioned; they are
# pinned to the same Khronos release so they cannot disagree.
#
# The loader is built but *not shipped*. Android exposes the phone's own
# libOpenCL.so as a vendor public library, and that one already knows where its
# driver is; ours exists so the NDK linker has the symbols to resolve against.
# Packaging it would shadow the real one with a loader that can find nothing —
# see the note in app/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt.
OpenCL-Headers        https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenCL-Headers     v2025.07.22 8a97ebc88daa3495d6f57ec10bb515224400186f
OpenCL-ICD-Loader     https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenCL-ICD-Loader  v2025.07.22 ad770a1b64c6b8d5f2ed4e153f22e4f45939f27f

# espeak-ng is Kokoro's front end, and it needs *compiled* data tables that its
# own build produces by running the espeak-ng binary — impossible when
# cross-compiling to Android. The tables are staged into assets instead, by
# tools/stage-espeak-data.py, which asserts their format version against the
# constant in this checkout's synthdata.c. Bumping the ref above means
# restaging: espeak refuses to load tables it did not compile.
#
# Kokoro's weights are not vendored at all. They are an ONNX graph downloaded
# through the in-app resolver like any other model, and ONNX Runtime arrives as
# a Maven AAR rather than a source checkout.
